  "notes": "Slot = 4 bytes {u8 id, u8 count, u8 0, u8 0}; write all 4 bytes (bytes 2-3 = 0). count 0xFF is displayed as infinite (verified). 8 slots usable (10 with the Side Pack; the array has 10 entries) plus a separate 11th 'special' slot right after (addr+0x28) holding Leon's Lighter (0x2F) / Claire's Lockpick (0x30). Ids 0x64-0x67 show 'no item'; 0x68+ are FILE documents, not inventory items. Counts and names update immediately (even with the status screen open), but the item ICON of a newly written id is not drawn in the status screen until it is loaded by the game (icon cell stays blank; the item still works: equipping a written R. Launcher via the menu put it in the EQUIP box with its count). HP is the player object's s16 HP (200 = full; Fine/Caution/Danger derived from it); max HP s16 at health.addr+0x0C (=200). Leon disc: equipped slot index u8 at 0xD5BF8 and equipped item id u8 at 0xD5BFA (observed changing 0->2 / 0x02->0x11 when equipping slot 3 via the menu; not write-tested). A second copy of the inventory exists at 0xDF398 (same layout; seems to be a room/save snapshot: writing it does NOT change the live inventory; write 0xD4A3C).",
  "verified": "2026-10-07 live: start inventory read [02 12][01 01] + special 2F 01 at 0xD4A3C matched the status screen (Hand Gun 18, Knife, Lighter: rei/re2_inv0.jpg). Wrote slot3=R. Launcher x4, slot4=H. Gun Bullets x60, slot5=F. Aid Spray, slot6=S. Machine Gun x255 -> status screen showed 4 / 60 / infinite and names (rei/re2_write_verify.jpg); equipped the R. Launcher (EQUIP box showed 4). HP: 0xCFD4E went 20->0 on death; wrote 200 -> CONDITION changed Danger->Fine (rei/re2_hp200.jpg). Name sweep rei/n2_A.jpg rei/n2_B.jpg. Frames are in the agent scratchpad (\u2026/scratchpad/rei/)."
